<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kassym-Jomart Tokayev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1953">1953</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kassym-Jomart Tokayev is a Kazakh diplomat and politician, formerly foreign minister, prime minister and Director-General of the UN Office at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a>. He became president of Kazakhstan in 2019 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nursultan-nazarbayev">Nursultan Nazarbayev</a> resigned. After the violent unrest of January 2022, put down with help from Russian-led troops, he removed Nazarbayev's family from power and introduced constitutional changes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kassym-jomart-tokayev.jpg" alt="Kassym-Jomart Tokayev" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: kremlin.ru · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kassym-Jomart_Tokayev_(2026-05-08)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
